# Railway — production follow-through

Railway **auto-deploys** from `main`. Do **not** watch / poll deployments (`list-deployments`, status loops, AwaitShell waits) after a routine commit/push — that burns credits for no gain.

## After push

- Stop at push confirmation unless the user asks about deploy status or the next step **requires** live production (MCP tool that only exists after deploy, re-seed `.data`, production health check they requested).
- Do **not** narrate “watching Railway” or sit on BUILDING/DEPLOYING for ordinary UI/lib commits.

## When production work is actually needed

- Prefer the **live Railway app** only when the user’s task needs production (new MCP tools, checklist apply on prod, screenshot upload to the volume, etc.).
- If you must know deploy state for that follow-through, check **once**; if still building, do other work or ask the user — do not busy-poll.
- On a **failed** deploy the user cares about, diagnose (logs / diagnosis) and fix or report.
- Ephemeral `.data` must be **re-seeded after deploy** when the task needs that data — do that when production is ready, not by watching every push.

## Tone

- Trust auto-deploy. Be proactive on **product** follow-through, not on deploy telemetry.
